{"actor_ref":"claude","class":"draft_history","document_uuid":"01a1a54a-312e-73f2-8e4c-d85491bf698d","id":"01a1a5dd-8936-74f8-aad5-c17611ccf66e","idempotency_key":"698b1f1fea0cd5e51140067baaf269af92b65d189f583e63e68c3e5968fc75de","occurred_at":"2026-11-04T09:22:01Z","payload":{"note":"Cross-board addressing works: AppCtx gained ai_session_id/ai_target_board, the Assistant publishes the selected session's target, and the strip marks that board (chip label '· AI target', .board-chip.target outline). When the target is not the visible board a dashed badge reads 'AI -> <title>' and clicking it selects that board, so focusing is an explicit request rather than a surprise jump. 'Set as AI target' targets the board you are looking at, which is also how an analysis position is handed over - there is no separate 'use this position' button. While testing this I found and fixed a real dead end: new_workspace only ever made a client-side tab with no server_id, so 'New board' on a fresh tab could only answer 'the workspace has no server side yet' and no board could be stored at all; the tab now creates its server workspace immediately. STILL OPEN: i-3b88 - the strip is the board list, but there is no separate left-rail board tree.","target":"t-f436"},"type":"work.note_added","v":2}
